{"name":"Opening Night","hex":"#bd6426","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"opening night","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The first night, evening, or day of a spectacle or show.","The first event in a new venue."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/opening_night"}],"entries":[{"title":"Premiere","blocks":[{"text":"A premiere, also spelled première, is the debut of a work, i.e. play, film, dance, musical composition, or even a performer in that work."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Premiere_at_Chinese_Theater_%283555047236%29.jpg/330px-Premiere_at_Chinese_Theater_%283555047236%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Premiere","wikidata":"Q204854"},{"title":"The Opening Night","blocks":[{"text":"The Opening Night is a 1927 American silent drama film directed by Edward H. Griffith and starring Claire Windsor, John Bowers and E. Alyn Warren."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/The_Opening_Night.png/330px-The_Opening_Night.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Opening_Night","wikidata":"Q94243345"},{"title":"Opening Night (1977 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Opening Night is a 1977 American psychological drama film written and directed by John Cassavetes, and starring Gena Rowlands, Ben Gazzara, Joan Blondell, Paul Stewart, Zohra Lampert, and Cassavetes. Its plot follows a stage actress who, after witnessing the accidental death of a fan, struggles through a nervous breakdown while she prepares for an upcoming Broadway premiere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Opening_Night_%281977_poster%29.jpg/330px-Opening_Night_%281977_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opening_Night_(1977_film)","wikidata":"Q1504568"},{"title":"Night","blocks":[{"text":"Night, or nighttime, is the period of darkness when the Sun is below the horizon. Daylight illuminates one side of Earth, leaving the other in darkness. The opposite of nighttime is daytime. Earth's rotation causes the appearance of sunrise and sunset. Moonlight, airglow, starlight, and light pollution dimly illuminate night. The duration of day, night, and twilight varies depending on the time of year and the observer's latitude."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/330px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night","wikidata":"Q575"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Pasadena_Civic_Auditorium_Oct_2016.jpg/500px-Pasadena_Civic_Auditorium_Oct_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Pasadena_Civic_Auditorium_Oct_2016.jpg/1280px-Pasadena_Civic_Auditorium_Oct_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Pasadena_Civic_Auditorium_Oct_2016.jpg/500px-Pasadena_Civic_Auditorium_Oct_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Filming took place primarily at the Pasadena Civic Auditorium","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APasadena_Civic_Auditorium_Oct_2016.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png/500px-Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png/500px-Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org